Description: Qualitatively code a corpus by asking a local language model a set
    of questions about each document and reading the answer from the model's
    next-token probability distribution rather than parsing its text. Extraction
    never fails to parse, returns a probability per label, and reports the
    probability mass the model placed outside the label set. Includes the
    auditing steps that separate usable annotation from plausible-looking
    output. These inspect the documents that fired on an item and draw blinded
    samples for human coding. Requires a running 'Ollama' server.
